providers/mana: drop a pending CQE that makes no progress

rdma-core v65 mana_poll_cq() keeps a CQE pending while its handler
reports consumed=false, and loops `while (num_polled < nwc)`. When
handle_rc_requester_cqe() gets an ACK whose PSN is not below qp->sq_psn,
advance_send_completions() returns 0 at once, yet the next shadow WQE
has end_psn <= psn, so consumed stays false. Nothing changes between
iterations: the poll never returns and holds the CQ spin lock. Observed
in racer on Azure MANA: the RDMA owner thread spun inside one
mana_poll_cq() call for the rest of the process lifetime.

Treat "produced nothing and not consumed" as consumed, which is what
v61 did with every CQE. A later cumulative ACK still completes the
send WQEs.

--- a/providers/mana/cq.c
+++ b/providers/mana/cq.c
@@ -566,6 +566,18 @@
 		ret = mana_handle_cqe(ctx, &cq->pending_cqe, &wc[num_polled], nwc - num_polled, &consumed);
 		num_polled += ret;
 
+		/* A CQE that produced nothing and asks to stay pending can never
+		 * make progress: retrying it with the same room spins forever with
+		 * the CQ lock held. Drop it like an unknown CQE; a later ACK covers
+		 * the same send completions, since ACK PSNs are cumulative.
+		 */
+		if (!consumed && ret == 0) {
+			verbs_warn_datapath(verbs_get_ctx(ibcq->context),
+					    "CQE wqid=%u made no progress: dropped\n",
+					    cq->pending_cqe.wqid);
+			consumed = true;
+		}
+
 		cq->has_pending_cqe = !consumed;
 	}
 
